  "title": "Charles Doolittle Walcott",
  "summary": "American paleontologist (1850-1927) who directed the U.S. Geological Survey from 1894 to 1907 and then served as Secretary of the Smithsonian Institution until his death. He is best known for finding the Burgess Shale fossils in the Canadian Rockies in 1909 and for collecting there for years afterward.",
